<!-- awf:section preamble -->
# {{ .prefix }}-brainstorming

Brainstorming owns clarification, design exploration, proportionate presentation, conditional grounding invocation, and final design approval. It does not create an effort.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section when-to-invoke -->
## When to invoke

Use only when behavior, scope, structure, dependencies, patterns, checks, or testing need a material choice or clarification. Proceed directly when the intended outcome, solution shape, affected boundary, and verification are already clear.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section procedure -->
## Procedure

1. **Orient in the topic.** Invoke `{{ .prefix }}-orienting` when its repository-truth moments apply, then run `awf context <relevant paths>`.
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->
2. Clarify the outcome and present proportionate alternatives and a recommendation.
3. If correctness depends on broad or uncertain repository premises, invoke `{{ .prefix }}-grounding`; it is advisory and does not create an effort.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section example-clarifying-questions -->
Ask focused questions one at a time and avoid inventing requirements.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section design-sections -->
Per `docs/maintainable-code-design.md`, settle the semantic model and ownership, representation boundaries, dependency direction, test seams, and preparatory-refactor decision in a proportionate simplicity contract: scope and exclusions, structural approach and dependencies, patterns or abstractions, and checks and testing strategy. A straightforward change may settle these in a few sentences rather than a fixed checklist. The final approved design becomes the implementation boundary.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section no-spec-rule -->
Do not create a separate specification. Put durable decisions in an ADR and useful sequencing in a plan when their independent triggers apply.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section terminal-step -->
Stop for final design approval. Once approved, independently evaluate whether an ADR, plan, effort, or implementation review is warranted; no later mechanism is automatic.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section definitions -->
A load-bearing decision remains meaningful after implementation.{{ with .data.loadBearingExamples }} Examples:{{ range . }} {{ .item }};{{ end }}{{ end }} A plan is warranted only when sequencing, coordination, or resumability materially helps.{{ with .data.errorBoundaries }} Consider configured error boundaries:{{ range . }} {{ .name }};{{ end }}{{ end }}
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section anti-patterns -->
Do not use line count, artifact type, or another mechanism firing as a trigger.
<!-- awf:end -->
